This is a repost of mine explaining how to get the Nethack playing screen to
look *just* like your home version.

Putty is a excellent program one can use to play Nethack in this month's
tourney.

I have gotten to the point that Putty makes my tourney game look exactly
like my out-of-the-box nethack home app.  I'm not saying these will or won't
work for you.

Ready?
1. Putty config.  NOTE - when you click all this stuff in, make sure you
save it in the "Saved sessions" window.  Once you save it, click *once* on
the saved session, and then the LOAD button to enter more settings, or
double-click to bring up a window in which to play on the tourney server.


"Session" defaults except:
- Hostname:    scheherazade.devnull.net
- Port:             22
- Protocol:     SSH
"Terminal" - all default values (Do NOT set keypad to "Nethack")
"Window/Appearance" defaults except:
- Font: !! Terminal/10 pt. !!  (IMPORTANT!!)
"Window/Translation" defaults except:
- Character set: CP437
"Connection" defaults except:
- Terminal-type string: xtermc
- Terminal speeds: 38400,38400  (default, but not sure if this will vary as
per provider's setup)


2. Nethack settings
(O)ptions
- Set "f - color" to true
- Set "n - IBMgraphics" to true
- Set number_pad to 1-On


